    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n57642" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					680
				</span></i>
			; imper. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.50
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				1068
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.</u>
				852
			</span></i> (both lyr.); subj.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίῃς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					1.311
				</span></i>
			; opt.
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.42
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				504
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κιοίτην, κίοιτε</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.149
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				3.347
			</span></i>; part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κιών, κιοῦσα</span> (for the accent cf.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰών</span>), <i><span class="en">
				4.427
			</span></i>, al.: impf.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκιον</span>, 
				Ep.
			1pl.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίομεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.456
				</span></i>
			:—<i>go</i>, in Hom.almost always of persons,
				<i><span class="en">
				2.565
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.471
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.427
			</span></i>, etc.; of ships, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.509
			</span></i>:— 
				Ep.
			 Verb, Trag. only <i><span class="en">
				A.
			</span></i>; as etym. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίνησις</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Cra.</u>
				426c
			</span></i>: in <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> perh. always aor., unless impf. in
				<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				23.257
			</span></i>. (Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κινέω, κίνυμαι</span>, Lat.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξιο.</span>)</div>
